    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build succeeds and all tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature for the PetClinic owner endpoints. An owner request may now include an optional `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR), and the owner response exposes a derived `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is supplied.\n\nChanges, following the project's established patterns for derived owner fields:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (source of the generated DTOs):\n   - Added `title` as an optional input on the `OwnerFields` schema.\n   - Added `salutation` as a read-only field on the `Owner` schema.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter, so the title survives `POST /api/owners` \u2192 `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n3. **`Salutations.java`** (new util) \u2014 composes the salutation: `title + \" \" + lastName` when a non-blank title is present, otherwise the last name alone (mirrors the other `util` derivation classes like `TelephoneDisplays`/`Localities`).\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the `salutation` mapping expression delegating to `Salutations.salutationFor(owner)`. The `title` field maps automatically (same name, both `String`) in both directions.\n\n5. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added a nullable `title` column to the `owners` table. The test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema.sql change is what actually provisions the column at test time.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` test (POST title=`DR`, lastName=`who` \u2192 GET `$.salutation` == `\"DR who\"`) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
